<Layout title="Lighthouses">
	<p>
		Before lighthouses ran on electricity, the keeper climbed the tower several times a night to
		trim the lantern wick. An untrimmed wick smoked and blackened the glass, and the light grew dim.
		When the fog came in thick enough to hide the beam, the keeper started the fog signal.
		<sup>
			<a href="#note">1</a>
		</sup>
	</p>
	<p id="note">
		The first fog signals were bells, rung by hand or by clockwork. Steam whistles and horns came
		later.
		<a data-footnote-backref href="#">
			Back to the text
		</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
